# imported at runtime (verified: no module under nodes/ or visual/ reads these
# paths; docs/ appears only inside error-message STRINGS). Readers get all of
# it on GitHub, where the README's relative links actually resolve.
CLAUDE.md
BUG_LOG.md
BUG_LOG_2026-06.md
session_handoff.md
docs/
kibitz-plugin/
tmp/

# 2026-09-01 (ship audit, registry-flag-06 / -12, fresh-install-docs-03 / -04):
# build metadata and maintainer-only files that were shipping to every
# installer. None of it is read at runtime (verified: no module under nodes/
# opens these paths). _START_HERE.md is the maintainer's own build routing
# with an absolute path on the operator's box; SKILL.md is the AI-assistant
# sprint process; workflows/external_examples/ are vendored third-party
# graphs carrying a stranger's absolute path, and nothing in nodes/ loads
# them (~380 KB). This file itself narrates the pack's scanner history and has
# no business in the scanned zip.
.comfyignore
.gitignore
.gitattributes
SKILL.md
_START_HERE.md
workflows/external_examples/

# 2026-09-03: the ledger viewer is HALF of a dev harness and the other half is
# already excluded. `viewer/index.html` fetches `/ledger?latest=1`, `/list` and
# `/ledger?path=`; the only thing that serves those routes is
# `scripts/serve_ledger.py`, which `scripts/*` above stops shipping. The pack's
# own registered route is `/otr/latest_ledger` (__init__.py) -- a DIFFERENT
# path. (This used to add "and it is gated behind
# OTR_ENABLE_HTTP_RENDER_ROUTES=1 besides", which was never true: that flag
# gated only the two POST render routes, which were REMOVED 2026-09-05. The
# ledger GET registers unconditionally on every install and always did.) So on
# a registry install every one of the page's three fetches 404s: it has shipped
# to every installer as a page that cannot work. It stays in git for the
# developers who run the server beside it.
viewer/

# 2026-09-04, on a fable pre-publish review: `tools/` is DEVELOPER tooling and
# nothing shipped imports it (grep clean across nodes/ and __init__.py), yet it
# was reaching the registry zip -- six .py files that no installer can use.
# One of them, `tools/engine_matrix.py`, sets OTR_TEST_MODE at import, so it
# also contributed an `os.environ` finding to the scan for a file that is not
# part of the product. Excluding it makes the scan's surface equal the pack's
# actual surface, which is the claim the manual-review request makes.
#
# `config/` is NOT excluded and must not be: `config/cast_pools.py` and its
# siblings are read at render time.
tools/

# 2026-09-05, bundle-hygiene rung 1 of the strip-down ladder
# (docs/GO_FORWARD_PLAN.md). Two groups that ship to every installer and that
# nothing a user runs ever reads. EXCLUDING FROM THE BUNDLE IS NOT DELETING
# FROM GIT, and here that distinction has teeth: `pyproject.toml` publishes the
# registry card art as a RAW GITHUB URL
# (.../v2.0-alpha/assets/otr_icon.gif), which the registry fetches from GitHub,
# never from the zip. A `git rm -r assets/` would therefore blank the listing's
# icon while this line costs nothing. Do not "finish the job" by deleting them.
#
# assets/ -- 1.8 MB of repo decoration. github-social-preview.jpg (830 KB) is a
# GitHub repository SETTING, otr_icon.gif (946 KB) and otr_icon.png are the
# registry card art served from GitHub raw, and radio_face_bookend.png is
# unread by anything (zero hits across nodes/, __init__.py, config/ and
# workflows/otr_canonical.json). Measured: the only `assets/` strings under
# nodes/ are two comments in otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py about filename
# whitespace.
assets/
#
# workflows/variants/*.md -- 92 generated LAUNCH RECIPES, one per variant,
# written by scripts/build_variants.py. Every one of them is a headless command
# built on runners under scripts/, which `scripts/*` above already stops
# shipping, so on a registry install they document commands the installer
# cannot run. THE .json VARIANTS THEMSELVES KEEP SHIPPING -- README's "Pick the
# graph" table tells a user to drag `workflows/variants/otr_*.json` onto the
# canvas, so this pattern is deliberately .md-only. Never widen it to
# workflows/variants/.
workflows/variants/*.md
